cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VoxDown or its specification, please cite it as below."
title: "VoxDown: Markdown for stories read aloud"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Etienne
    family-names: Ackermann
    alias: eackermann
    website: "https://github.com/eackermann"
abstract: >-
  VoxDown is a plain-text format for stories that are read aloud: a Markdown
  story with light marks for who says each line, how they say it, the sounds a
  listener hears, where the pages turn, and notes for the performer. This
  repository holds the specification with its conformance examples, a parser,
  HTML views, an editor, a command-line tool and a VS Code extension.
repository-code: "https://github.com/voxdown/voxdown"
url: "https://voxdown.github.io/"
keywords:
  - voxdown
  - markdown
  - audiobook
  - text-to-speech
  - screenwriting
  - plain-text format
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-09"
